    q: "The brain is a surprisingly expensive organ to run. It makes up only around 2 per cent of an adult's body weight. ----. Much of this is thought to be spent not on conscious effort but on the constant background signalling between nerve cells. For this reason, the brain's energy use changes relatively little between solving a difficult puzzle and simply sitting quietly.",
